The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
if (sk->sk_bound_dev_if || exact_dif) {
    bool dev_match = (sk->sk_bound_dev_if == dif || sk->sk_bound_dev_if == sdif);
    if (exact_dif && !dev_match)
        return -1;
    if (sk->sk_bound_dev_if && dev_match)
        score += 4;
}
```
Reason:
The condition `if (!dev_match)` allowed mismatches in the device interface to occur without causing an error, which broke the expected behavior of the `SO_BINDTODEVICE` option. This change meant that the bound device interface did not need to match, leading to incorrect socket behavior.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (!dev_match)
    return -1;
if (sk->sk_bound_dev_if)
    score += 4;
```
Reason:
By removing the `exact_dif` check and ensuring that any mismatch in the device interface results in an immediate return of `-1`, the patch reinstates the requirement that the bound device interface must match the socket's bound device interface, thus restoring the expected semantics of `SO_BINDTODEVICE`.

